            "kind": "mechanism",
            "alt": "Step 1: nucleophilic attack of CH3CH2NH2 on the carbonyl carbon of CH3CH2COCl, giving a tetrahedral intermediate with O- and N+ bearing H"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "figure",
            "id": "s2",
            "src": "q03_s2.svg",
            "kind": "mechanism",
            "alt": "Step 2: tetrahedral intermediate with O- and N+ rearranges, Cl- leaves, giving CH3CH2C(=O)N+H(H)CH2CH3 ion"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "figure",
            "id": "s3",
            "src": "q03_s3.svg",
            "kind": "mechanism",
            "alt": "Step 3: Cl- takes H+ from the N+ ion, giving the amide CH3CH2CONHCH2CH3 and HCl"
